# One helper copies for many classes, so at its parameters the prototype objects of all of them have met, and so have the literals. What is copied where is told apart at the calls.
# A copy whose ends are captures of its function is taken up to the function that makes the closure, one whose ends are parameters to each call that enters the function: both ends by the same call. There the ends are the call's own operands.
# `extend` is handed the function and reads `prototype` off it: the end is the function, and stands for its prototype object.
